\tag{fnip}
\title{Equilibria and the current–voltage relation}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The [Hodgkin–Huxley system](fnip-0071) balances an applied
current against three ionic currents. In that system, the
equations for #{n}, #{m}, and #{h} are an
[activation equation](fnip-0071) multiplied by the temperature
factor #{\phi}. The
Morris–Lecar velocity of \ref{fnip-0005} balances an applied
current against three ionic currents, and the equation for #{n} is
an [activation equation](fnip-0071) multiplied by the positive
factor #{\phi}.}

\p{For which applied currents is there one equilibrium, and for
which applied currents are there three?}

\transclude{fnip-0075}
